---
/**
 * The shipped admission path for one roast, drawn.
 *
 * This is the order the route actually runs in (`src/app/api/roast/route.ts`):
 * rate limit, parse, bot check or session, daily budget, collect, compute,
 * generate, store. The outcome column is editorial labelling, not a
 * measurement, and no step here is claimed to be faster or slower than another.
 */
---

<figure class="pipe">
  <div class="pipe__head">
    <span class="pipe__label">How one verdict gets made</span>
    <span class="pipe__note">Schematic: the shipped admission order</span>
  </div>

  <div class="pipe__entries">
    <div class="pipe__entry">
      <span class="pipe__entry-kind">Demo defendant</span>
      <p class="pipe__entry-text">
        Three fabricated personas. No account, no sign-in, and the finished verdict is cached
        for an hour.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="pipe__entry">
      <span class="pipe__entry-kind">Your account</span>
      <p class="pipe__entry-text">
        Google sign-in with one read-only scope. Likes, subscriptions and playlist titles are
        read once, then the token is discarded.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="pipe__merge">
    <span>Both entries meet the same gate:</span>
  </p>

  <ol class="pipe__steps">
    <li class="pipe__step">
      <span class="pipe__index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div class="pipe__body">
        <p class="pipe__row">
          <span class="pipe__title">Rate limit</span>
          <span class="pipe__tag">abuse</span>
        </p>
        <p class="pipe__detail">
          Three roasts per hour per IP, checked before the request body is even parsed.
          Rejected requests never write, so hammering cannot extend the window.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="pipe__step">
      <span class="pipe__index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div class="pipe__body">
        <p class="pipe__row">
          <span class="pipe__title">Bot check or session</span>
          <span class="pipe__tag">identity</span>
        </p>
        <p class="pipe__detail">
          A demo request passes Cloudflare Turnstile. A real roast needs a sealed session
          cookie, and a missing secret fails closed instead of waving requests through.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="pipe__step">
      <span class="pipe__index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div class="pipe__body">
        <p class="pipe__row">
          <span class="pipe__title">Daily budget</span>
          <span class="pipe__tag">cost</span>
        </p>
        <p class="pipe__detail">
          One counter for the whole site, fifteen roasts a day by default. When it is spent,
          the answer is a 429 with a sentence a person can read.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="pipe__step">
      <span class="pipe__index" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
      <div class="pipe__body">
        <p class="pipe__row">
          <span class="pipe__title">Collect and compute</span>
          <span class="pipe__tag">evidence</span>
        </p>
        <p class="pipe__detail">
          Liked videos, subscriptions and playlist titles come back from the YouTube Data
          API, then become ordinary numbers: shorts ratio, topic entropy, late-night count,
          a lurker index.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="pipe__step">
      <span class="pipe__index" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
      <div class="pipe__body">
        <p class="pipe__row">
          <span class="pipe__title">Score in code</span>
          <span class="pipe__tag">scoring</span>
        </p>
        <p class="pipe__detail">
          The Brain Rot Score is arithmetic over those signals. The model never sets it, and
          its opinion of the score is overwritten if it tries.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="pipe__step">
      <span class="pipe__index" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
      <div class="pipe__body">
        <p class="pipe__row">
          <span class="pipe__title">Model writes the roast</span>
          <span class="pipe__tag">language</span>
        </p>
        <p class="pipe__detail">
          Gemini returns the headline, the roast body, the red flags, the channel verdicts
          and the share line against a response schema, and nothing else.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="pipe__step">
      <span class="pipe__index" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
      <div class="pipe__body">
        <p class="pipe__row">
          <span class="pipe__title">Store the verdict</span>
          <span class="pipe__tag">sharing</span>
        </p>
        <p class="pipe__detail">
          The report is written once under a random id, so the link a reader shares keeps
          working. There is no TTL, which is why deletion is a request a person makes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <figcaption class="pipe__caption">
    Read in either direction: the top is what a visitor experiences, the bottom is what the
    route has to survive before the joke reaches the page.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .pipe {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .pipe__head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.4rem 1rem;
  }

  .pipe__label {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .pipe__note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  /* Nested resets so the article page's prose rules for lists and paragraphs do
     not reshape the ledger inside this figure. */
  .pipe .pipe__entries {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1.15rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .pipe__entry {
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .pipe__entry-kind {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .pipe .pipe__entry-text {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .pipe .pipe__merge {
    position: relative;
    margin: 1.15rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .pipe .pipe__merge::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    right: 0;
    left: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--color-card-border);
  }

  .pipe .pipe__merge span {
    position: relative;
    padding-right: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
  }

  .pipe .pipe__steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: none;
  }

  .pipe .pipe__step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.1rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .pipe .pipe__step + .pipe__step {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
  }

  .pipe__index {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  .pipe .pipe__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.3rem 0.7rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pipe__title {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .pipe__tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
  }

  .pipe .pipe__detail {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .pipe .pipe__caption {
    margin: 1.05rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .pipe {
      padding: 1.2rem 1rem 1rem;
    }

    .pipe .pipe__entries {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .pipe .pipe__step {
      grid-template-columns: 1.7rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.7rem;
    }
  }
</style>
